    <statement><p>Evaluate the following.</p>
<p><m>\displaystyle{ \left\lvert-15.76\right\rvert= }</m> <fillin characters="6" name="AnSwEr0001"/></p>
</statement>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>15.76</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
    <solution><p>The absolute value of <m>-15.76</m> is the distance between <m>-15.76</m> and <m>0</m> on the number line. In this case, since <m>-15.76</m> is <m>15.76</m> units away from 0, the answer is <m>15.76</m>.</p>
</solution>
